# Line endings: LF in the repository, LF in every working tree.
#
# Learned the hard way. A rename sweep rewrote three files whole and flipped
# their endings — one of them from CRLF to LF, two of them the other way — which
# buried 34 lines of real change under ~550 lines of pure noise in review, and
# left one file disagreeing with the other 190. Nothing declared an ending, so
# nothing could catch it.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text (so the PNG under docs/ is left
# alone) and `eol=lf` fixes the answer for everything that is.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Spelled out rather than left to detection: a binary asset that gets
# normalised is corrupted, and the failure shows up as a broken image much later.
*.png binary
